      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 28: one implementation to rule the harnesses — dedup, package rename, layout",
      "text": "Yes: every duplicated function was proven bit-identical (or a strict superset) against real ride data before deletion, then the fast harnesses and the full bootstrap_ci gate battery were re-run and matched. Net effect: one Python implementation of the engines/parsers (src/bicycling_energy_model/), the retired V8-exactness machinery deleted (v8math.py, ~460 lines), and the JS parity harness (analysis/parity/) retired to git history since its job — proving the Python port equals the JS it replaced — is done. The repo was also restructured (src/, research/journal/, data/inputs|results/) for cohesion; zero behavioural change.",
